<title>USA: IPO HIGHLIGHTS - Pameco gains.</title>
<headline>IPO HIGHLIGHTS - Pameco gains.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pameco Corp shares rose over 20 percent to 16-7/8 on the company's first day of trading on the New York Stock Exchange, with more than two million shares exchanging hands by the early afternoon.</p>
<p>Around 3.6 million shares were offered at $14 each in a deal lead-managed by Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette.</p>
<p>Pameco is a distributor of heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems, as well as of equipment and refrigeration products.</p>
<p>Antivirals Inc's deal of two million units, each consisting of one common share and one warrant, was priced at $9 a unit.   The common shares were at 6-3/4 in early</p>
<p>afternoon trading while the warrants were at 2-1/4.</p>
</text>
